# Workflow: GML8W

This document shows how to run LLM model in GGUF format with llama-cpp backend engine

## 1. Context

- **Working directory**: `~/echo-home/workstation/lmstudio/gmlama`
- **OS/Kernel**: Windows

## 2. Model Inventory

### Entry format

Format: `<MODEL_ID>:<MODEL_NAME>: ["<MODEL_DESCRIPTION>", "<LLAMACPP_PARAMS>"]`

Description:

- MODEL_ID: index number to select model
- MODEL_NAME: Name of model in gguf
- MODEL_DESCRIPTION: Prefix `GPU/` is to run with GPU, otherwise with CPU 
- LLAMACPP_PARAMS: parameters of llama-cli

## 3. Commands

| Command                                      | Description                 |
| -------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- |
| `cd ~/echo-home/workstation/lmstudio/gmlama` | Set working directory       |
| `gml8w --help`                               | list model entries          |
| `gml8w <MODEL_ID>`                           | run model with specified ID |

## 4. Workflows

### Run model from inventory

```makefile
list_model:
    # Description: View inventory to select model id
    # Command: `gml8w --help`
    # Success: output list of entries in model inventory
    # Failure: no entry found
    # Output: <MODEL_ID>
start_model: list_model
    # Description: start a model by selected model id
    # Command: `wingterm gml8w <MODEL_ID>`
    # Success: no error
    # Failure: any error
test_port: start_model
    # Description: test LLM port
    # Command: `curl  http://localhost:<PORT>/v1/models`
    # Success: output of model name
    # Failure: any error
    # Input: <PORT> specified in `LLAMACPP_PARAMS`
```
